  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": 0,
      "title": "Prepare digestion mix",
      "instruction": "Prepare fresh digestion mix (15 min). Optionally make batches of five non‑resuspended mixes in a 50 mL Falcon tube and store at 4 °C if enzymes are stable. Weigh and combine 19 U Dispase and 5 000 U Collagenase IV in a 50 mL Falcon tube, resuspend in 10 mL aDMEM, filter through a 0.22 µm filter, then add 10 µg DNase I and 10 µL of 1 mM Y‑27632.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 1,
      "title": "Collect organoids for scRNA‑seq",
      "instruction": "Remove dead cells and harvest intact organoids (1–3 h). Inspect the organoid culture plate under brightfield microscopy to confirm organoid formation. Using a wide‑bore pipette tip (e.g., P1000), carefully transfer organoids to a new Falcon tube, avoiding single cells that remain at the well bottom. Re‑inspect the plate to ensure no organoids remain; repeat the transfer if substantial groups are left.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 2,
      "title": "Dissociate organoids and prepare single‑cell suspension",
      "instruction": "Dissociate the collected organoids using the same enzymatic protocol applied during organoid passaging, then process the cells for single‑cell RNA sequencing.",
      "substeps": [
        {
          "instruction": "Centrifuge cells or organoids at 350 g for 5 min in spinning buckets.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Apply the enzymatic digestion (as prepared in Step 1) to dissociate organoids.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Transfer the resulting cell suspension into ice‑cold PBS containing 1 % BSA.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Count the cells.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Optional: If overall viability is 2,000 cells post‑processing).",
          "title": ""
        }
      ],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    }
  ],
  "verification_status": "literature_sourced",
  "normalised_at": "2026-06-19T01:10:37.807329Z",
  "llm_normalised": true,
  "description": "See the full list of reagents in the key resources table. Perform all centrifugation steps of cells and organoids at 350 g for 5 min in spinning buckets. As this protocol includes human tissues, verify that you comply with applicable local, institutional and national regulations. Ensure that required approvals, consent documentation, and ethical clearances are in place prior to initiating the work. In the context of our specific study, informed consent is obtained from each enrolled patient before sample collection, under an approval by the Ethics Committee of Northwestern and Central Switzerland (EKBB/EKNZ 37/13). While this protocol describes the steps for Matrigel-free organoid culture conditions, a subset of advanced prostate cancer samples may grow successfully and expand in classical Matrigel-based conditions (as pointed in our study1). Particularly in the case of metastasis samples, we advise to grow the samples in both Matrigel-free and Matrigel-based conditions, whenever possible. For the latter, we refer the readers to seminal works reporting Matrigel-based culture for PCa PDOs.2,3,4,5,6 All the subsequent steps for organoid characterization can be applied for both culture condition systems.",
